==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Great Angel Chibinel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*2 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Boraphim]] spawns as the boss once 50 Cat Units have been defeated.

==Strategy==
Using fast units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]] and talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] with [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|manic]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|meatshields]] should do most of the work. The Boraphim is only at 100% magnification, so basic [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] attackers should be enough. [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] is a good pick, but wait to deploy them until the Boraphim appears since they are expensive and slow. However, you also have to hope that the Surge Base doesn't wipe out your units too many times.

Units with [[Kamikaze]] like [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] also perform excellently here, as they can tank damage from enemies and take the hits from Surge Base, and their vanishment don't contribute to the total Cat Units defeated counter, preventing Boraphim from spawning too soon. Additionally, strong units that don't rely on lots of spamming (like replacing meatshields with [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to tank Li'l Bun Buns), or Surge-immune units, can greatly slow down the counter, allowing you to even destroy the base before Boraphim shows up at all. Timing Stone Cat to block the Surge Base's initial hit also helps with this, and it's pretty easy, just deploy Stone right when the Surge Base's light glows blue.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]]: Extremely bulky while also being able to do very high DPS, Dioramos can Knockback and Slow Boraphim (in the case that his Surge Attack is triggered).
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Lucifer]]: Strong Against the Floating and Angel enemies on this stage, while also being Immune to Surge.

==Trivia==
*A bug involving how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn in if they're not counted as boss enemies, discovered in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]], made it possible for the Surge Base to attack the Cat Base on this stage. This was fixed in [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], which increased the width of this stage by 100.

